{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540468003,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNzM5MDcxNDA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2948","origin":"github"},"title":"Dataset ID and checkout --orphan","message":"Our dataset ID actually is bound to a branch, since it is committed in `.datalad/config`.\nIn context of PR #2946 this leads to an interesting question. Therein `test_run.py:test_rerun_just_one_commit` fails, because `rerun` complains, that the original run record was ran from a different dataset. This is because the dataset id is in master and the test checks out an orphan branch to operate on. Now `rerun` compares the original dataset id to `None` (no `.datalad/config` in that branch) and fails. There's a little bit more details to that test failures regarding what is reevaluted at what point in time, but that's not the point.\n\nThe point is: Such branch would get a different dataset id than 'master' one way or another (including even no id at all unless `create` is also called on that branch). I think that's fine, since the orphan branch actually has no common history with master. But it might have weird side effects. What do you think - do we want it that way, @mih , @yarikoptic , @kyleam ? Otherwise datalad id needs to go into `.git/config` instead, I guess.","files":null}]}